WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.879
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.880 --> 00:08.175
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.175 --> 00:11.969
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.970 --> 00:14.847
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.848 --> 00:18.226
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.227 --> 00:21.646
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.647 --> 00:23.064
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.065 --> 00:24.690
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.691 --> 00:31.072
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:38.997 --> 00:41.542
Fake news.

01:05.691 --> 01:08.067
Here you go, guys. A little hot coffee.

01:08.068 --> 01:09.569
Where'd we even go last night?

01:09.570 --> 01:11.195
I have no idea.

01:11.196 --> 01:13.197
- Cup of coffee, Joe?
- Yeah. Thanks.

01:14.449 --> 01:16.784
I remember we got
really excited about something.

01:16.785 --> 01:19.370
That's right, that's right, we had that
million-dollar business idea.

01:19.371 --> 01:21.622
- Does anyone remember it?
- More coffee, Joe?

01:21.623 --> 01:23.499
Sure, I'll take another cup.

01:23.500 --> 01:25.710
Didn't anyone write it down?

01:25.711 --> 01:28.171
Wait a minute, maybe it's in my pocket.

01:29.715 --> 01:32.258
Peter, are you just rubbing
pocket cloth over your wang?

01:32.259 --> 01:35.553
I'm actually popping a leg
pimple, mister smarty pants.

01:35.554 --> 01:38.097
Damn it, I'm sick of us always
forgetting our great ideas

01:38.098 --> 01:39.140
when we're drinking.

01:39.141 --> 01:41.058
Well, down at work, we wear body cams.

01:41.059 --> 01:43.102
We could just do that
when we're drinking.

01:43.103 --> 01:45.021
That's a great idea, Joe.

01:45.022 --> 01:47.440
Thanks. Now maybe you'll
take down those three billboards

01:47.441 --> 01:49.109
you put up about me.

01:57.159 --> 01:59.035
That's not true.

02:07.252 --> 02:09.003
Wow, Joe, these are pretty cool.

02:09.004 --> 02:11.631
Yeah, they're not as heavy
as I thought they'd be.

02:11.632 --> 02:14.216
And we can live stream
the footage on my iPad.

02:14.217 --> 02:15.760
How do we talk when they're on?

02:15.761 --> 02:16.886
Like, different?

02:16.887 --> 02:19.555
No, Peter.
Use your normal speaking voice.

02:19.556 --> 02:21.265
- All right, let's hit it.
- Hang on, guys.

02:21.266 --> 02:23.894
I'm just gonna say goodbye to Lois.

02:26.271 --> 02:27.938
<i>Where the hell
do you think you're going?</i>

02:27.939 --> 02:30.024
<i>I told you, I'm going
to the Clam with the guys.</i>

02:30.025 --> 02:31.692
<i>Oh, surprise, surprise.</i>

02:31.693 --> 02:33.361
<i>Another night out with the losers.</i>

02:33.362 --> 02:36.489
<i>Losers?! Name five
things wrong with each of them.</i>

02:36.490 --> 02:38.116
<i>With pleasure.</i>

02:39.743 --> 02:42.536
Lois sends her love. Come on, let's go.

02:42.537 --> 02:44.955
What does she mean,
"Can't eat an ear of corn"?

02:44.956 --> 02:47.750
I can't help it
if my adult teeth never came in.

02:47.751 --> 02:49.960
<i>She says I call Steinfeld Steinfeld?</i>

02:49.961 --> 02:52.463
Of course I do, that's his name.
Jerry Steinfeld.

02:52.464 --> 02:55.675
<i>Pardon me, to quote his famous bit.</i>

02:55.676 --> 02:57.802
<i>She says I say erverybody weird?</i>

02:57.803 --> 03:01.055
<i>I say erverybody just like
erverybody else does.</i>

03:01.056 --> 03:02.807
You do say that weird.

03:10.065 --> 03:12.942
<i>This Sunday,
we turn the Quahog Convention Center</i>

03:12.943 --> 03:14.694
<i>into a mud pit</i>

03:14.695 --> 03:17.363
<i>for the 28th annual Quahog
Monster Truck Rally</i>

03:17.364 --> 03:18.989
<i>and gun show.</i>

03:18.990 --> 03:21.909
<i>See giant monster trucks.
Shoot at monster trucks!</i>

03:21.910 --> 03:24.412
<i>And best of all, you can smoke inside.</i>

03:24.413 --> 03:26.956
<i>See the Ghost Rider
while smoking inside.</i>

03:26.957 --> 03:29.834
<i>Fire an AR15 while smoking inside.</i>

03:29.835 --> 03:32.586
<i>Or just stand around and smoke inside.</i>

03:32.587 --> 03:33.963
<i>Seriously, we're cool with it.</i>

03:33.964 --> 03:36.590
<i>Throw your butts on the ground.
We don't care.</i>

03:36.591 --> 03:38.843
<i>Watch real loud trucks
and smell the smoke</i>

03:38.844 --> 03:41.178
<i>that reminds you of your
dead alcoholic stepdad</i>

03:41.179 --> 03:43.723
<i>who you're glad is dead
but still miss anyway.</i>

03:43.724 --> 03:45.349
<i>Rest in peace, Gene.</i>

03:45.350 --> 03:47.351
<i>Forget which beer can is your ashtray.</i>

03:47.352 --> 03:50.771
<i>And whenever you feel like it,
shout racial stuff.</i>

03:50.772 --> 03:53.315
<i>You will not be
the fattest person there,</i>

03:53.316 --> 03:55.968
<i>and if you are, get that shirt off!</i>

03:55.969 --> 03:58.237
<i>Come get your picture taken
with Tila Tequila,</i>

03:58.238 --> 04:00.030
<i>and smoke a cigarette with her.</i>

04:00.031 --> 04:03.200
<i>Spray soda on somebody. Punch a baby.</i>

04:03.201 --> 04:06.036
<i>Smoke inside. Loud trucks, guns.</i>

04:06.037 --> 04:08.122
<i>It's all happening at the
Quahog Convention Center,</i>

04:08.123 --> 04:11.667
<i>so hold in all your farts till
this Sunday, Sunday, Sunday!</i>

04:11.668 --> 04:12.793
<i>Farts.</i>

04:12.794 --> 04:14.503
All right, here we go.

04:14.504 --> 04:16.422
Million-dollar business ideas.

04:16.423 --> 04:19.425
Open forum, no self-editing.
Wide-open slate.

04:19.426 --> 04:21.051
No such thing as a bad idea.

04:21.052 --> 04:22.803
- Beer in a bag.
- Bad idea.

04:22.804 --> 04:24.889
Oh, oh, I got one. Big Tic Tac,

04:24.890 --> 04:27.183
so you don't have to eat
so many little Tic Tacs.

04:27.184 --> 04:28.517
Nice, Glenn, you're on the board.

04:28.518 --> 04:30.394
All right, any ideas. No bad ideas.

04:30.395 --> 04:32.062
- Soup in a sleeve.
- Bad idea.

04:32.063 --> 04:33.898
All right, Peter, you're so great,

04:33.899 --> 04:35.608
why don't you give us an idea?

04:35.609 --> 04:37.818
Okay, you know how they
put ice in urinals?

04:37.819 --> 04:40.154
Well, what happens to that ice
at the end of the day?

04:40.155 --> 04:42.490
It's wasted. We collect urinal ice

04:42.491 --> 04:44.074
and sell it to local bars.

04:44.075 --> 04:45.409
Peter, that'll never work.

04:45.410 --> 04:47.411
Oh, no?

04:47.412 --> 04:51.458
<i>Is that the tinkling of ice I hear?</i>

04:55.128 --> 04:57.713
All right, let's check out
what we did last night.

04:57.714 --> 04:59.799
God, that's so shaky.

04:59.800 --> 05:01.133
It's hard to watch.

05:01.134 --> 05:02.718
What is that one?

05:02.719 --> 05:06.222
That's mine.
I'm basically a human Steadicam.

05:06.223 --> 05:09.058
- It's beautiful.
- So smooth.

05:09.059 --> 05:10.559
Lot of guy butts.

05:10.560 --> 05:12.937
Yeah, my sight line's
a little lower than most.

05:12.938 --> 05:14.271
Look at a girl butt once.

05:14.272 --> 05:16.148
What the hell were we doing here?

05:16.149 --> 05:18.818
Oh, this must have been
when we were jumping around

05:18.819 --> 05:21.362
to "Jump Around,"
like the song asked us to.

05:21.363 --> 05:23.113
Oh, yeah, I was so into this song.

05:23.114 --> 05:25.491
Look at my footage. I was going bananas.

05:25.492 --> 05:27.327
All right, let's
fast-forward a little here.

05:30.789 --> 05:33.624
Just looks like we're drinking
at a random bar.

05:33.625 --> 05:36.377
We ain't talking about
any million-dollar ideas.

05:36.378 --> 05:38.462
Wait, wait, pause it.
Zoom in on that napkin.

05:38.463 --> 05:39.506
What does that say?

05:41.758 --> 05:43.926
There it is. "Warm cuts."

05:43.927 --> 05:45.636
Like cold cuts, but warm.

05:45.637 --> 05:47.513
Our million-dollar idea.

05:47.514 --> 05:49.139
Warm cuts? That's dumb.

05:49.140 --> 05:52.643
<i>If it's so dumb, how come
we're pitching it on Shark Tank?</i>

05:52.644 --> 05:54.270
<i>Now, when we first started Warm Cuts,</i>

05:54.271 --> 05:55.938
<i>it was just a gross idea.</i>

05:55.939 --> 05:58.399
<i>But this year,
we're on track to get sued</i>

05:58.400 --> 06:00.693
<i>for $12.5 million.</i>

06:00.694 --> 06:02.611
<i>That's quadruple the projections.</i>

06:02.612 --> 06:04.530
<i>You know what, I like your product.</i>

06:04.531 --> 06:07.157
<i>But more than that, I like you guys.</i>

06:07.158 --> 06:10.578
<i>I'm in, and I'll give you
exactly what you're asking for:</i>

06:10.579 --> 06:14.164
<i>$100,000 for ten percent.</i>

06:14.165 --> 06:16.292
<i>What do you say?</i>

06:16.293 --> 06:18.711
<i>Does anyone other
than Robert have an offer?</i>

06:18.712 --> 06:21.213
<i>Wait, why are only three
of us on Shark Tank?</i>

06:21.214 --> 06:22.506
Yeah, where's Quagmire?

06:22.507 --> 06:24.217
Oh, my God, is that...

06:27.052 --> 06:28.596
Quagmire, you hooked up.

06:28.597 --> 06:30.139
All right.

06:30.140 --> 06:32.391
Oh, no, wait, wait. It's on film.

06:32.392 --> 06:35.060
That's not all right.
What if my boss sees this?

06:35.061 --> 06:36.478
What if my dad sees it?

06:36.479 --> 06:39.189
It's fine, Glenn.
You can't even see your face.

06:39.190 --> 06:42.610
<i>You did it again, Glenn Quagmire.</i>

06:42.611 --> 06:45.404
Oh, my God. Joe,
you have to delete this footage.

06:45.405 --> 06:47.698
Sorry, Glenn, the footage is
automatically uploaded

06:47.699 --> 06:49.366
to the Internet every night.

06:49.367 --> 06:51.745
The Internet?! Oh, my God.

06:54.539 --> 06:57.625
Excuse me, ma'am, no porn at the bar.

06:57.626 --> 06:59.293
Oh, it's okay, I'm transgender.

06:59.294 --> 07:01.045
Oh, I-I had no idea.

07:01.046 --> 07:03.631
Do whatever you want all the time.

07:03.632 --> 07:06.216
Oh, Glenn...

07:06.217 --> 07:07.718
Howdy, stranger.

07:07.719 --> 07:09.887
Brian? What are you doing here?

07:09.888 --> 07:12.097
- I'm an alcoholic.
- Oh, right.

07:12.098 --> 07:13.807
So, you saw the video, huh?

07:13.808 --> 07:16.352
Oh, yeah. It's just so hard.

07:16.353 --> 07:18.062
Well, it has to be for sex.

07:18.063 --> 07:19.396
No, no, I mean-I mean it's difficult

07:19.397 --> 07:22.107
to watch your son embarrass
himself so publicly.

07:22.108 --> 07:25.194
Yeah, that parent-child
relationship is so special.

07:25.195 --> 07:27.154
Sometimes you want
to shake 'em by the shoulders

07:27.155 --> 07:29.073
and say, "Aah, what are you doing?"

07:29.074 --> 07:31.408
But you just got to give 'em
the biggest hug you can

07:31.409 --> 07:33.911
and let 'em know that you'll
always be there for them.

07:33.912 --> 07:35.537
- How's your son, Brian?
- We don't talk.

07:35.538 --> 07:37.373
But, Ida, you can't blame yourself.

07:37.374 --> 07:39.917
As much as you want to save
your kids from their mistakes,

07:39.918 --> 07:42.544
it's their mistakes that
help them grow and change

07:42.545 --> 07:44.046
and become their best selves.

07:44.047 --> 07:46.256
You know, Brian,
that's what I like about you.

07:46.257 --> 07:48.425
You're so wise and kind.

07:48.426 --> 07:50.471
I think that's what
originally drew me to you.

07:50.472 --> 07:53.263
Yep, here I am, Mr. Wisdom,

07:53.264 --> 07:55.182
sitting at the bottom of a bottle,

07:55.183 --> 07:56.725
just like every Tuesday.

07:56.726 --> 07:58.936
- Brian, it's Thursday.
- Oh, boy.

07:58.937 --> 08:01.188
Why do you always run yourself down?

08:01.189 --> 08:02.856
You're handsome, you're loyal.

08:02.857 --> 08:05.025
You give your paw
after a couple of tries.

08:05.026 --> 08:07.069
Come on, paw.

08:07.070 --> 08:10.489
Paw. Paw...

08:10.490 --> 08:12.616
There you go. Good boy.

08:12.617 --> 08:15.744
I just wish you could see
yourself the way I see you.

08:15.745 --> 08:17.496
Ehh, mirrors kind of freak me out.

08:17.497 --> 08:20.290
And-and funny, too.

08:20.291 --> 08:22.126
Except for a job and your own home,

08:22.127 --> 08:24.504
you are the full package, Brian Griffin.

08:25.839 --> 08:28.966
Ida... should we get a room?

08:28.967 --> 08:30.844
Absolutely.

08:33.096 --> 08:36.307
They've got
one person working back there.

08:37.892 --> 08:39.560
Morning, sleepyhead.

08:39.561 --> 08:41.562
- Morning.
- Some night, huh?

08:41.563 --> 08:42.980
Yeah, it really was.

08:42.981 --> 08:45.482
<i>They dropped a USA Today
outside our room.</i>

08:45.483 --> 08:47.151
- You want to read it?
- Oh, God, no.

08:47.152 --> 08:49.486
Well, I guess we'll pretend
this never happened,

08:49.487 --> 08:51.238
and I'll see you in another two years.

08:51.239 --> 08:52.865
Yeah.

08:52.866 --> 08:55.159
You know what? No.

08:55.160 --> 08:57.036
What are you doing Friday night?

08:57.037 --> 08:58.162
Well, that depends.

08:58.163 --> 09:00.039
<i>Is Friday Night Videos still a thing?</i>

09:00.040 --> 09:01.957
No, it hasn't been for quite some time.

09:01.958 --> 09:03.292
Well, then, I'm free.

09:03.293 --> 09:05.252
Does that mean you're asking me out?

09:05.253 --> 09:06.462
I guess it does.

09:06.463 --> 09:09.006
You're... not ashamed to be with me?

09:09.007 --> 09:10.841
No, I'm not. I don't care anymore.

09:10.842 --> 09:13.886
I guess I'm just not as hung up
as I used to be.

09:13.887 --> 09:15.512
Room service.

09:15.513 --> 09:16.930
Oh, my God, you ordered room service?!

09:16.931 --> 09:18.098
Are you crazy?

09:18.099 --> 09:19.475
What if somebody finds out I'm in here

09:19.476 --> 09:21.602
having goofball sex?

09:21.603 --> 09:23.520
Hello? Room service.

09:23.521 --> 09:25.022
I've got your eggs and Snausages.

09:25.023 --> 09:27.069
Snausages.

09:34.449 --> 09:36.867
Table 13. The fish is for the gentleman,

09:36.868 --> 09:38.285
and the chicken is for the lady.

09:38.286 --> 09:39.621
Got it.

09:41.039 --> 09:42.956
Great. Is that our food?

09:42.957 --> 09:45.042
<i>The fish is for the gentleman,</i>

09:45.043 --> 09:47.878
<i>and the chicken is for the lady.</i>

09:47.879 --> 09:50.422
I'll be right back, folks.

09:50.423 --> 09:52.174
Well, thanks for picking me to break in

09:52.175 --> 09:53.509
your new Discover card with.

09:53.510 --> 09:55.177
Hey, thanks for co-signing for it.

09:55.178 --> 09:56.805
My pleasure.

10:01.309 --> 10:03.352
Brian, I can't help but notice

10:03.353 --> 10:06.355
you're a little uncomfortable
spending time with me.

10:06.356 --> 10:08.232
I thought you said
you weren't ashamed of me.

10:08.233 --> 10:09.525
What are you talking about?

10:09.526 --> 10:11.235
Because I made you lie down
in the back seat

10:11.236 --> 10:13.237
all the way here? You looked tired.

10:13.238 --> 10:14.905
It just seems like
you're always taking me

10:14.906 --> 10:17.533
to out-of-the-way places
to avoid being seen together.

10:17.534 --> 10:20.077
- Like yesterday.
- Come on, that's not true.

10:20.078 --> 10:22.372
I just wanted to show you
a beautiful view.

10:23.873 --> 10:27.876
Wow, check out that big blue marble.

10:27.877 --> 10:29.211
Look, there's another shuttle.

10:29.212 --> 10:30.505
Get away from the window!

10:36.386 --> 10:38.387
<i>Okay, maybe, maybe this has been</i>

10:38.388 --> 10:40.556
a little weirder for me than I thought.

10:40.557 --> 10:42.558
I'm sorry, Ida. I...

10:42.559 --> 10:45.853
I really care about you
and you deserve better.

10:45.854 --> 10:48.272
- Can I help you?
- The fish is for...

10:48.273 --> 10:51.441
The fish is for me. And the chicken...

10:51.442 --> 10:55.029
the chicken is for
my girlfriend, Ida Davis.

10:57.031 --> 10:59.700
"Girlfriend"? Are you sure, Brian?

10:59.701 --> 11:01.201
I'm sure.

11:01.202 --> 11:03.912
And from now on,
I'm not hiding anything.

11:03.913 --> 11:06.833
Like Peter and his formaldehyde jars.

11:08.751 --> 11:11.086
- Peter?
- Yes?

11:11.087 --> 11:13.505
Is this is about my work?

11:13.506 --> 11:16.508
Hi, I have a Styrofoam cooler
with weird tape on it?

11:16.509 --> 11:20.470
Ah, that must be the cat brains
and baby bodies.

11:20.471 --> 11:22.973
Are you making people?

11:22.974 --> 11:25.225
He'll be flattered you called him that.

11:32.400 --> 11:34.902
Hello, everybody.

11:34.903 --> 11:36.904
I have some pretty big news.

11:36.905 --> 11:40.407
- It may come as a surprise, but...
- It's about Ida, isn't it?

11:40.408 --> 11:43.076
It has to be. Why else
would Ida be in our house?

11:43.077 --> 11:45.245
Meg's right.
I-Ida's only been here, what,

11:45.246 --> 11:47.581
- like, twice her whole life?
- You think they did it again?

11:47.582 --> 11:50.500
- Well, what else could it be?
- They do have a lot in common.

11:50.501 --> 11:52.753
Two mature people
with dwindling options.

11:52.754 --> 11:54.755
Like, I know Brian was
squeamish about sleeping

11:54.756 --> 11:57.758
with a trans woman before,
but it's 2019 now.

11:57.759 --> 12:00.928
Yeah, things that were gross
five years ago are now heroic.

12:00.929 --> 12:04.473
Wow. Brian and Ida. Good for them.

12:04.474 --> 12:05.933
Well, that's a relief.

12:05.934 --> 12:08.685
Now the only other person we
have to tell about us is Glenn.

12:08.686 --> 12:11.021
Oh, God, I haven't
even thought about that.

12:11.022 --> 12:13.523
Mr. Quagmire hates Brian.

12:13.524 --> 12:15.150
Yes, my big brother's right.

12:15.151 --> 12:17.069
Quagmire thinks Brian's trash.

12:17.070 --> 12:18.862
Well, just have him
over here for dinner.

12:18.863 --> 12:21.531
We'll help you.
We're here for you, Brian.

12:21.532 --> 12:24.034
You know what? You're right.
I can do this.

12:24.035 --> 12:26.787
After all, I'm not the first
person to deliver tough news.

12:26.788 --> 12:28.830
Like when they found Waldo.

12:28.831 --> 12:31.458
There are many things
I can't go into at this time,

12:31.459 --> 12:33.794
but I can confirm
that a body was removed

12:33.795 --> 12:35.837
from Waldo's apartment this morning.

12:35.838 --> 12:37.923
Is this being treated as a suicide?

12:37.924 --> 12:39.925
Again, I can't confirm.

12:39.926 --> 12:43.220
But to that point, instead of
always asking "Where's Waldo?"

12:43.221 --> 12:46.556
maybe some of you should've been
asking "How's Waldo?"

12:46.557 --> 12:48.309
Good day.

12:53.273 --> 12:55.065
Glenn, Ida, it's so nice

12:55.066 --> 12:57.067
that you could both
come over for dinner.

12:57.068 --> 12:58.777
Thanks so much for having us.

13:03.283 --> 13:05.575
No response from Peter. What the hell?

13:05.576 --> 13:07.411
I thought we were going to the Clam.

13:07.412 --> 13:10.080
And Quagmire just texted back "Can't."

13:10.081 --> 13:11.581
I don't like it.

13:11.582 --> 13:14.001
They're doing something without us.

13:14.002 --> 13:17.629
So, Brian, what's, uh,
what's new in your world?

13:17.630 --> 13:19.840
Oh, well, um,

13:19.841 --> 13:21.675
thank you for asking, Lois.

13:21.676 --> 13:23.844
- I see them.
- They're both in there.

13:23.845 --> 13:25.512
Looks like a dinner party!

13:25.513 --> 13:29.016
Uh, actually, I have some news
that happens to pertain

13:29.017 --> 13:31.101
- to my dating life.
- Really, Brian?

13:31.102 --> 13:33.103
- Oh, do tell us.
- I knew it!

13:33.104 --> 13:35.647
Well, it's kind of big news.

13:35.648 --> 13:37.400
Those scalloped potatoes?

13:37.401 --> 13:39.026
Well, what's the big news?

13:39.027 --> 13:41.445
Go ahead, Brian. Tell him.

13:41.446 --> 13:43.488
Ida and I...

13:43.489 --> 13:45.407
have, uh...

13:45.408 --> 13:46.783
begun dating.

13:46.784 --> 13:49.286
You're, you're joking, right?

13:49.287 --> 13:52.122
It's true, son. Brian and I are in love.

13:52.123 --> 13:54.624
What?! When were you gonna tell me this?

13:54.625 --> 13:57.085
Oh, Peter just texted.

13:57.086 --> 13:58.754
He says he's stuck at work.

13:58.755 --> 14:03.217
They are working that poor man to death.

14:08.222 --> 14:11.391
I'm so glad you dropped in.
Brian is cooking breakfast.

14:11.392 --> 14:14.144
That's right, get ready
for Eggs a la Brian.

14:14.145 --> 14:16.480
Scrambled eggs with a side of toast.

14:16.481 --> 14:19.608
What? How is that "a la Brian"?
That, that's just...

14:19.609 --> 14:22.319
That's, that's great.
That's just great, Brian.

14:22.320 --> 14:25.155
I am very excited
for this unique breakfast.

14:25.156 --> 14:27.908
Cool, cool. How many globs
of ketchup do you want?

14:27.909 --> 14:29.409
Uh, chef's choice.

14:29.410 --> 14:33.622
So, um, how long
has this been going on, Dad?

14:33.623 --> 14:36.583
Listen, Glenn, I know
this is an adjustment for you,

14:36.584 --> 14:39.586
and you and Brian haven't
always seen eye to eye.

14:39.587 --> 14:41.088
Well, I wouldn't say that.

14:41.089 --> 14:44.508
He's just, uh, kind of
a big personality.

14:44.509 --> 14:46.343
So, Denver Airport.

14:46.344 --> 14:49.012
Kind of up there, huh? Mile-high.

14:49.013 --> 14:51.515
Yeah, that is the height of the airport.

14:51.516 --> 14:54.851
Now, O'Hare Airport,
why on the ticket is it "ORD"?

14:54.852 --> 14:57.187
Uh, it was originally called
Orchard Field.

14:57.188 --> 14:58.688
Really? Huh.

14:58.689 --> 15:01.191
Uh, so why is
Wilkes-Barre/Scranton "AVP"?

15:01.192 --> 15:03.735
I'm not gonna go through
every airport with you, Brian.

15:03.736 --> 15:06.029
You know, Glenn, Brian thought
you two could hang out

15:06.030 --> 15:08.323
this afternoon,
and I think that's a great idea.

15:08.324 --> 15:10.200
Yeah, Quagmire, what do you say?

15:12.537 --> 15:14.871
All right. I guess I can do that.

15:14.872 --> 15:16.039
Well, great.

15:16.040 --> 15:17.374
Oh, the ketchup's hot.

15:17.375 --> 15:19.798
Everyone goes cold, I go hot.

15:19.799 --> 15:22.338
And that's the "a la."

15:25.258 --> 15:27.993
This sucks. I don't want to be here.

15:27.994 --> 15:29.886
Come on, Glenn.
If I'm gonna be dating your mom,

15:29.887 --> 15:31.805
it's important that we spend
some time together.

15:31.806 --> 15:35.601
Hi, we have two guest passes
from a museum member, Ida Davis.

15:37.145 --> 15:39.121
I'm not seeing an "Ida Davis."

15:39.122 --> 15:41.106
Uh, try "Dan Quagmire."

15:41.107 --> 15:43.692
- "Lieutenant Dan Quagmire."
- Ah, the lieutenant.

15:43.693 --> 15:45.694
And how's he doing?
Still have his penis?

15:45.695 --> 15:47.028
No, he doesn't.

15:47.029 --> 15:48.864
And that's a weird question to ask.

15:48.865 --> 15:51.117
I'm a weird guy, I work at a museum.

15:53.911 --> 15:56.157
See? It's not so bad.

15:56.158 --> 15:58.126
<i>It's like Night at the Museum in here.</i>

15:58.127 --> 16:00.061
- How?
- Well, you know,

16:00.062 --> 16:01.543
like, the guys are gonna come to life.

16:01.544 --> 16:04.421
- Like, who?
- Um, the guys, you know?

16:04.422 --> 16:06.214
When it's, when it's nighttime.

16:06.215 --> 16:08.216
- You didn't see the movie, did you?
- No.

16:08.217 --> 16:09.718
Why did you bring up
a reference to something

16:09.719 --> 16:11.052
you know nothing about?

16:11.053 --> 16:13.430
I... it just, it reminded me of, uh...

16:13.431 --> 16:15.098
Brian, don't bring up
a reference to someone

16:15.099 --> 16:16.516
whose favorite movie it is,

16:16.517 --> 16:18.393
because you'll just embarrass yourself.

16:18.394 --> 16:20.061
That was a natural history museum,

16:20.062 --> 16:21.688
this is a science museum.

16:21.689 --> 16:24.065
What, you think this tidal
chart's gonna come to life?

16:24.066 --> 16:26.443
You think this moon rock
is gonna walk across the room

16:26.444 --> 16:28.445
and riff brilliantly like Robin Williams

16:28.446 --> 16:31.239
playing Teddy Roosevelt,
God rest both their souls?

16:31.240 --> 16:35.119
<i>Be very, very careful treading
around Night at the Museum.</i>

16:40.419 --> 16:43.084
Okay, let's get this game started.

16:43.085 --> 16:45.545
- Do you believe it still fits?
- From when?

16:45.546 --> 16:47.714
Thank you for throwing this barbecue.

16:47.715 --> 16:50.678
It's so good for the boys
to spend real time together.

16:50.679 --> 16:54.096
Okay, let's play.
Kids versus the parents.

16:55.182 --> 16:56.973
All right, we're gonna
destroy those kids.

16:56.974 --> 16:58.975
Uhp, someone's on the wrong team.

16:58.976 --> 17:01.645
Boy, they're in such a hurry
not to be kids anymore.

17:01.646 --> 17:03.730
Your time will come, trust me.

17:03.731 --> 17:06.066
I'm older than the adults.
I'm older than all of you!

17:06.067 --> 17:08.235
It seems like that sometimes, I bet.

17:08.236 --> 17:11.113
Get down there, champ.

17:13.449 --> 17:16.159
All right, as the one adult
on a team full of children,

17:16.160 --> 17:17.494
I'm gonna act good-natured

17:17.495 --> 17:19.996
while being subtly furious
at all your mistakes.

17:19.997 --> 17:21.581
Okay? Break on three.

17:21.582 --> 17:23.649
One, two, three...

17:23.650 --> 17:24.793
- Break!
- Football!

17:24.794 --> 17:27.337
Let's focus, Chris.
Can we just focus for a minute?

17:27.338 --> 17:30.336
And let's all face the same direction.

17:30.337 --> 17:31.633
Okay, I'm gonna call the plays

17:31.634 --> 17:34.427
while I'm covering my mouth
with this play card.

17:34.428 --> 17:37.138
Peter, that's not a play card,
it's a Denny's menu.

17:37.139 --> 17:40.348
Let's run Moons Over My Hammy on three.

17:40.349 --> 17:43.103
Hey, guys? Gonna need
your help over here.

17:43.104 --> 17:45.730
They got a real All-American at QB.

17:45.731 --> 17:46.856
God.

17:46.857 --> 17:48.400
Down. Hut! Hut!

17:48.401 --> 17:50.151
Good hutting, Glenn.
That's my boy, hutting.

17:50.152 --> 17:51.570
Way to hut!

17:51.571 --> 17:54.239
Shut up. Stop complimenting
things that don't need it.

17:54.240 --> 17:56.445
Hike!

18:00.913 --> 18:03.707
Uh-oh, look who's on the loose.

18:03.708 --> 18:05.750
I'm gonna get you, I'm gonna get you...

18:05.751 --> 18:08.420
Oh, no, I missed you by total accident.

18:08.421 --> 18:11.089
Yeah! Six points, bitches.

18:11.090 --> 18:13.967
Whoa, that was some great move, buddy.

18:13.968 --> 18:15.760
Aw.

18:15.761 --> 18:17.429
Did you see and hear the wink?

18:17.430 --> 18:19.472
That means he did it on purpose.

18:19.473 --> 18:21.641
No, no, way. He did it all by himself.

18:22.810 --> 18:24.102
Ah! There it is again!

18:24.103 --> 18:26.563
Brian, you're the best dad ever.

18:26.564 --> 18:27.981
What're you talking about? I beat him.

18:27.982 --> 18:30.191
I wish I had a dad like that.

18:30.192 --> 18:31.943
Me, too, bud.

18:31.944 --> 18:34.404
Brian, you're very sweet to do that.

18:34.405 --> 18:36.573
To do what? I'm the one
who scored the touchdown.

18:36.574 --> 18:39.576
- You sure did, Glenn.
- He's not my dad!

18:39.577 --> 18:42.370
I already have a dad, and
it's my mom! All right, Brian?

18:42.371 --> 18:44.707
Stop trying to be my dad, you fraud.

18:46.787 --> 18:48.918
Glenn, sweetie, calm down.

18:48.919 --> 18:51.924
No, I'm not gonna calm down.
I can't take this anymore.

18:51.925 --> 18:53.923
Listen, Dad, the first time
you hooked up with Brian,

18:53.924 --> 18:55.508
it was awful, I hated it.

18:55.509 --> 18:58.219
But you were confused, you'd
just gone through a huge change,

18:58.220 --> 19:01.139
you didn't know if you had
any options, so you settled.

19:01.140 --> 19:03.558
But you're a beautiful,
intelligent woman.

19:03.559 --> 19:06.561
And now you've had time to
adjust and your choice is Brian?

19:06.562 --> 19:09.022
Why in God almighty
would you choose him?

19:09.023 --> 19:12.192
"Because I love him,"
a resolved Ida said.

19:12.193 --> 19:14.736
- I'm also a published author.
- Self-published.

19:14.737 --> 19:16.446
You're also a pompous, pretentious,

19:16.447 --> 19:17.947
hypocritical blowhard.

19:17.948 --> 19:20.283
- Who attended Brown.
- For one semester.

19:20.284 --> 19:22.202
- You went to Brown?
- For two months.

19:22.203 --> 19:23.703
See? See, that's what I mean.

19:23.704 --> 19:25.497
His whole life is a lie.

19:25.498 --> 19:28.584
I can't take this anymore.
It's either him or me.

19:35.299 --> 19:37.550
- I choose Brian...
- Yes.

19:37.551 --> 19:39.678
To talk to first.

19:39.679 --> 19:42.681
Brian, I've loved every minute
that we've spent together.

19:42.682 --> 19:44.307
I never thought I'd meet someone

19:44.308 --> 19:46.810
who I connected with on so many levels,

19:46.811 --> 19:49.145
- much less an Ivy Leaguer.
- Come on...

19:49.146 --> 19:53.274
But as special as you are to me,
I have to put my son first.

19:53.275 --> 19:55.485
- But Ida...
- He's my son.

19:55.486 --> 19:57.570
I've made my decision.

19:57.571 --> 19:59.322
Bye-bye, Brian. You're history.

19:59.323 --> 20:02.659
And this time, history's
not coming back to life.

20:02.660 --> 20:04.619
<i>Night at the Museum.</i>

20:04.620 --> 20:06.121
I'm sorry, Brian.

20:06.122 --> 20:08.748
I'll never forget what we had together.

20:08.749 --> 20:11.043
I understand.

20:12.795 --> 20:14.462
Can you guys wrap this up?

20:14.463 --> 20:17.298
I see Peter coming with some
kind of problem from the game.

20:17.299 --> 20:20.969
Quagmire, we agreed
that it was a two-hand touch,

20:20.970 --> 20:23.722
and then Chris hit me with one hand,

20:23.723 --> 20:25.473
and I said that didn't count,

20:25.474 --> 20:27.434
but he still wouldn't
count the touchdown.

20:27.435 --> 20:29.602
So I drilled him in the head
with the ball,

20:29.603 --> 20:31.187
and now he's not moving.

20:31.188 --> 20:33.940
He can blink his eyes, but nothing else.

20:33.941 --> 20:37.235
- So, is my dog still your dad?
- Uh, no.

20:37.236 --> 20:40.817
Chris, he said the touchdown counts!

20:40.818 --> 21:41.818
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv